Installed `VirtualList` (`@/components/ui/virtual-list`), a thin React wrapper over [React Virtuoso](https://github.com/petyosi/react-virtuoso) 4.18.16 (`react-virtuoso`, MIT). Every Virtuoso prop and handle method works as documented by Virtuoso; the look is unchanged.

```tsx
import { VirtualList, type VirtuosoHandle } from "@/components/ui/virtual-list";

const list = React.useRef<VirtuosoHandle>(null);

<VirtualList
  aria-label="Orders"
  data={orders}
  itemContent={(index, order) => <OrderRow order={order} />}
  ref={list}
  style={{ height: 480 }}
/>

list.current?.scrollToIndex({ index: 0, behavior: "smooth" });
```

What the wrapper adds: list semantics with each row's position in the whole list, a focus ring on the scroll region and the region role when it is named, and reduced-motion scrolling (smooth scrolls jump). Give the list a height (or `useWindowScroll`), a name, and `initialItemCount` if it should render rows on the server. Only the MIT `react-virtuoso` package is used. Wraps React Virtuoso by Petyo Ivanov (MIT); the license notice is at the end of the file.
